{
  "raw": {
    "https://ufv.njoyn.com/CL3/xweb/xweb.asp?clid=56144&Page=JobDetails&Jobid=J1026-0239&BRID=364393&lang=1": {
      "title": "Coordinator, Academic Communications, Faculty of Science",
      "description": "Job postings > Careers | UFV.ca Future Students International Current Students Alumni Academic Calendar myUFV myClass Library UFV / Careers Job postings To display this page you need a browser with JavaScript support. Share Facebook X Email LinkedIn Coordinator, Academic Communications, Faculty of Science Office of the Dean Abbotsford (King Road) Application deadline: October 22, 2026 Job Number: J1026-0239 Status: Temporary Open Positions: 1 Salary Schedule: Staff Salary Schedule, Group 7 Hours/Week: 35 Salary: $31.33 - $37.43/Hour Position Description Job Summary The Academic Communications Coordinator is actively involved in engaging with external stakeholders and incorporating community input to develop and adjust programs within the faculty area. Additionally, they build and maintain relationships with external stakeholders to expand education opportunities and identify potential partnerships with community organizations. The Coordinator supports the Dean’s office on agreements and partnerships, and provides administrative support to Faculty Council and various subcommittees. This position is responsible for maintaining the faculty area’s website and social media accounts, creating promotional materials for events, and coordinating event planning from concept to completion. Qualifications Bachelor's degree from a recognized post-secondary institution. Minimum of two (2) years related experience in a post-secondary institution, or similar organization. Excellent written and oral communication skills, including website writing, editing and marketing and promotions. Strong problem solving and critical thinking skills. Demonstrated professionalism and ability to maintain confidentiality. Ability to remain calm under pressure. Strong interpersonal skills and the ability to work creatively and effectively as a member of a team. Proven success in developing and maintain positive working relationships with internal and external partners. Experience in agenda preparations, note-taking, transcription and follow-up for large meetings. Event planning experience is preferred. Knowledge of Microsoft Office Knowledge of editing and maintaining website content. How To Apply Please submit your resume and cover letter by the application deadline. About UFV The University of the Fraser Valley is located on the traditional territory of the Halq'eméylem-speaking peoples. We express our gratitude and respect for the honour of living and working in Stó:lo Tém:éxw (Stó:lo Land; Stó:lo World). In all that we do, UFV strives to support and honour the Stó:lo peoples goals of self-determination and well-being on these lands. A commitment to Indigenization and Reconciliation is core to our institutional Vision and Integrated Strategic Plan: IYAQAWTXW — which means House of Transformation. This commitment includes the goal of centering Indigenous ways of knowing throughout our organization, recognizing our responsibilities to community, and a multi-year plan to increase the number of Indigenous faculty, staff, and administrators working at UFV. UFV has campus locations in Abbotsford, Chilliwack, Mission, and Hope in the beautiful British Columbia, and in Chandigarh, India. Recognized as one of BC's top employers, UFV offers a combination of career and lifestyle benefits. Join a team of 1,400 passionate professionals who value integrity, inclusivity and excellence. At UFV, you will serve a vibrant community and shape the future of 15,000 students. Indigenization, equity, and diversity are essential to our work as a university. A diverse community fosters the inclusion of voices that have been historically underrepresented and marginalized. At UFV, we are committed to recruiting a diverse workforce that represents the community we proudly serve. We encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, members of groups that experience discrimination due to race, colour, place of origin, ancestry, and/or religion, persons who identify as women and 2SLGBTQ+, and persons with disabilities. We invite applicants to complete a confidential self-identification survey as part of the application process. All questions are voluntary, with an option to decline to answer. Information will be used to support efforts to broaden the diversity of the recruitment process, and results are not shared with the selection committee. Inquiries about the survey may be directed to careers@ufv.ca. Learn more about our commitment to diversity and inclusion. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. In an effort to be both environmentally and fiscally responsible, UFV will contact only candidates receiving an interview. We thank all applicants for considering UFV for employment. Shortlisted applicants may be required to undergo a criminal record check and/ or a verification of their education credentials. UFV is committed to the principle of equity in employment. Please note: you should receive a confirmation email once you have successfully applied to this position. If you do not, please contact the Njoyn Help Desk at webhelp.njoyn or 1-877-427-7717 Monday to Friday 8am to 8pm (EST). Are you interested in this job? Job Opportunities Career Alert My Profile Help 1-604-854-4554 careers@ufv.ca Future students Academic Calendar Find your program How to Apply Book a tour Transfer credits Tuition & fees FAQs Help Ask a question A to Z websites Course Finder Directory IT Service Desk Reset your password myUFV Search Current Students Advising Centre Bookstore Register for courses Safe Student Community Shuttle bus Student services Timetables myClass About us Accreditation Careers at UFV Cascades Athletics Make a gift Events Human Resources News Contact us Contact Us 1-604-504-7441 1-888-504-7441 Toll-Free Maps Ask a question Copy link ✓ Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More…"
    },
    "https://ufv.njoyn.com/CL3/xweb/xweb.asp?clid=56144&Page=JobDetails&Jobid=J1026-0045&BRID=364230&lang=1": {
      "title": "Research Assistant II (Peace and Reconciliation Centre)",
      "description": "Job postings > Careers | UFV.ca Future Students International Current Students Alumni Academic Calendar myUFV myClass Library UFV / Careers Job postings To display this page you need a browser with JavaScript support. Share Facebook X Email LinkedIn Research Assistant II (Peace and Reconciliation Centre) Research & Graduate Studies Chilliwack (CEP) Application deadline: October 21, 2026 Job Number: J1026-0045 Status: Temporary Contract Term: Nov 2026 - March 2027 Open Positions: 1 Salary Schedule: Staff Salary Schedule, Group 8 Hours/Week: 14 Salary: $35.14 - $41.91/Hour Position Description Job Summary The Research Assistant II works under the supervision of the Director, Peace and Reconciliation Centre (PARC), and supports community-engaged research, educational programming, knowledge mobilization, and reconciliation initiatives associated with the Stó:lo Peoples. The incumbent performs advanced research, project coordination, stakeholder engagement, facilitation, evaluation, and administrative functions in support of project objectives. The incumbent works collaboratively with Indigenous communities, Stó:lo partners, researchers, students, and project stakeholders. The incumbent exercises cultural sensitivity, discretion, and sound judgement when working with Indigenous communities and research participants and provides project-specific guidance and support to students, volunteers, and other project personnel. Qualifications Undergraduate degree in Indigenous Studies, History, Anthropology, Sociology, Criminology, Political Science, Education, Social Work, Geography, Peace and Conflict Studies, Communications, or another relevant discipline from a recognized postsecondary institution. Demonstrated knowledge of Indigenous histories, reconciliation, decolonization, cultural humility, or community-engaged research. Minimum of two (2) years related experience supporting research, community-engaged projects, educational initiatives, or reconciliation-related work. Demonstrated knowledge of Indigenous histories, reconciliation, decolonization, cultural humility, or community-engaged research. Experience conducting interviews, focus groups, community consultations, or stakeholder engagement activities. Proficient in Microsoft Office applications including Word, Excel, Outlook PowerPoint, Teams, and related technologies. Strong research, analytical, and writing skills, and experience preparing reports and knowledge mobilization materials. Demonstrated experience with working respectfully with Indigenous communities and organizations. Strong research, analytical, and writing skills, including experience preparing reports and knowledge mobilization materials. Experience conducting interviews, focus groups, community consultations, or stakeholder engagement activities. Experience using qualitative and/or quantitative research methods and software. Ability to work independently under minimal supervision, exercising good judgement and initiative. Excellent interpersonal, facilitation, and communication skills. Demonstrated organizational and time-management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. Ability to deal sensitively, effectively, and professionally with students, staff, faculty and research participants. Ability to handle sensitive information in a confidential and professional manner. Well-developed interpersonal skills and written and oral communication skills. Strong reviewing, proofreading, editing, and formatting skills. Ability to learn and apply sound research techniques, methodology and logical critical analysis. Experience organizing and supporting research meetings, events and activities is required. Ability to work flexible hours, including evenings and/ or weekends as required. Ability to travel to off-site locations as required. Access to reliable transportation may be required for off-site field work. How to Apply Please submit your resume and cover letter by the application deadline. About UFV The University of the Fraser Valley is located on the traditional territory of the Halq'eméylem-speaking peoples. We express our gratitude and respect for the honour of living and working in Stó:lo Tém:éxw (Stó:lo Land; Stó:lo World). In all that we do, UFV strives to support and honour the Stó:lo peoples goals of self-determination and well-being on these lands. A commitment to Indigenization and Reconciliation is core to our institutional Vision and Integrated Strategic Plan: IYAQAWTXW — which means House of Transformation. This commitment includes the goal of centering Indigenous ways of knowing throughout our organization, recognizing our responsibilities to community, and a multi-year plan to increase the number of Indigenous faculty, staff, and administrators working at UFV. UFV has campus locations in Abbotsford, Chilliwack, Mission, and Hope in the beautiful British Columbia, and in Chandigarh, India. Recognized as one of BC's top employers, UFV offers a combination of career and lifestyle benefits. Join a team of 1,400 passionate professionals who value integrity, inclusivity and excellence. At UFV, you will serve a vibrant community and shape the future of 15,000 students. Indigenization, equity, and diversity are essential to our work as a university. A diverse community fosters the inclusion of voices that have been historically underrepresented and marginalized. At UFV, we are committed to recruiting a diverse workforce that represents the community we proudly serve. We encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, members of groups that experience discrimination due to race, colour, place of origin, ancestry, and/or religion, persons who identify as women and 2SLGBTQ+, and persons with disabilities. We invite applicants to complete a confidential self-identification survey as part of the application process. All questions are voluntary, with an option to decline to answer. Information will be used to support efforts to broaden the diversity of the recruitment process, and results are not shared with the selection committee. Inquiries about the survey may be directed to careers@ufv.ca. Learn more about our commitment to diversity and inclusion. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. In an effort to be both environmentally and fiscally responsible, UFV will contact only candidates receiving an interview. We thank all applicants for considering UFV for employment. Shortlisted applicants may be required to undergo a criminal record check and/ or a verification of their education credentials. UFV is committed to the principle of equity in employment. Please note: you should receive a confirmation email once you have successfully applied to this position. If you do not, please contact the Njoyn Help Desk at webhelp.njoyn or 1-877-427-7717 Monday to Friday 8am to 8pm (EST). Are you interested in this job? Job Opportunities Career Alert My Profile Help 1-604-854-4554 careers@ufv.ca Future students Academic Calendar Find your program How to Apply Book a tour Transfer credits Tuition & fees FAQs Help Ask a question A to Z websites Course Finder Directory IT Service Desk Reset your password myUFV Search Current Students Advising Centre Bookstore Register for courses Safe Student Community Shuttle bus Student services Timetables myClass About us Accreditation Careers at UFV Cascades Athletics Make a gift Events Human Resources News Contact us Contact Us 1-604-504-7441 1-888-504-7441 Toll-Free Maps Ask a question Copy link ✓ Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More…"
    },
    "https://ufv.njoyn.com/CL3/xweb/xweb.asp?clid=56144&Page=JobDetails&Jobid=J0926-1003&BRID=364387&lang=1": {
      "title": "Analyst II, Systems (Applications)",
      "description": "Job postings > Careers | UFV.ca Future Students International Current Students Alumni Academic Calendar myUFV myClass Library UFV / Careers Job postings To display this page you need a browser with JavaScript support. Share Facebook X Email LinkedIn Analyst II, Systems (Applications) IT Services - Applications Abbotsford (King Road) Application deadline: October 22, 2026 Job Number: J0926-1003 Status: Permanent Open Positions: 1 Salary Schedule: IT Professional Salary Schedule, Group 4 Hours/Week: 35 Salary: $89,203.20 - $106,854.07/Year Position Description Job Summary The Analyst II, Systems is responsible for complex troubleshooting and problem solving of systems used by students, staff and faculty across the University. The Analyst II, Systems responds to complex technical issues and actively participates in the development of long-term business application and enterprise (ERP) system projects. The incumbent values both team success and individual achievement and champions a culture of continuous improvement. Qualifications Bachelor’s Degree in computer science or a related field. Minimum of six (6) years of experience in programming and integrating applications; preferably in a web environment. Familiarity to business/enterprise applications such as, Ellucian Banner, Blackboard, Infosilem and Transact is an asset, HTML, CSS, Groovy/Java, PHP, Python, Javascript and automation scripting is required. Ability to provide technical assistance and advice to peers and the user community Knowledge of database principals and APIs (Application Programming Interfaces). Demonstrated knowledge and use of Oracle SQL, PLSQL , Microsoft SQL and LDAP /Active Directory. Experience in project management is an asset. Experience designing, building, install, configuring and supporting applications on Linux and Windows Operating Systems. Ability to work effectively as a member of a team. Ability to proactively provide communication and customer service to users, vendors, and other key stakeholders. Demonstrated commitment to continuous learning and professional development. How to Apply Please submit your resume and cover letter by the application deadline. About UFV The University of the Fraser Valley is located on the traditional territory of the Halq'eméylem-speaking peoples. We express our gratitude and respect for the honour of living and working in Stó:lo Tém:éxw (Stó:lo Land; Stó:lo World). In all that we do, UFV strives to support and honour the Stó:lo peoples goals of self-determination and well-being on these lands. A commitment to Indigenization and Reconciliation is core to our institutional Vision and Integrated Strategic Plan: IYAQAWTXW — which means House of Transformation. This commitment includes the goal of centering Indigenous ways of knowing throughout our organization, recognizing our responsibilities to community, and a multi-year plan to increase the number of Indigenous faculty, staff, and administrators working at UFV. UFV has campus locations in Abbotsford, Chilliwack, Mission, and Hope in the beautiful British Columbia, and in Chandigarh, India. Recognized as one of BC's top employers, UFV offers a combination of career and lifestyle benefits. Join a team of 1,400 passionate professionals who value integrity, inclusivity and excellence. At UFV, you will serve a vibrant community and shape the future of 15,000 students. Indigenization, equity, and diversity are essential to our work as a university. A diverse community fosters the inclusion of voices that have been historically underrepresented and marginalized. At UFV, we are committed to recruiting a diverse workforce that represents the community we proudly serve. We encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, members of groups that experience discrimination due to race, colour, place of origin, ancestry, and/or religion, persons who identify as women and 2SLGBTQ+, and persons with disabilities. We invite applicants to complete a confidential self-identification survey as part of the application process. All questions are voluntary, with an option to decline to answer. Information will be used to support efforts to broaden the diversity of the recruitment process, and results are not shared with the selection committee. Inquiries about the survey may be directed to careers@ufv.ca. Learn more about our commitment to diversity and inclusion. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. In an effort to be both environmentally and fiscally responsible, UFV will contact only candidates receiving an interview. We thank all applicants for considering UFV for employment. Shortlisted applicants may be required to undergo a criminal record check and/ or a verification of their education credentials. UFV is committed to the principle of equity in employment. Please note: you should receive a confirmation email once you have successfully applied to this position. If you do not, please contact the Njoyn Help Desk at webhelp.njoyn or 1-877-427-7717 Monday to Friday 8am to 8pm (EST). Are you interested in this job? Job Opportunities Career Alert My Profile Help 1-604-854-4554 careers@ufv.ca Future students Academic Calendar Find your program How to Apply Book a tour Transfer credits Tuition & fees FAQs Help Ask a question A to Z websites Course Finder Directory IT Service Desk Reset your password myUFV Search Current Students Advising Centre Bookstore Register for courses Safe Student Community Shuttle bus Student services Timetables myClass About us Accreditation Careers at UFV Cascades Athletics Make a gift Events Human Resources News Contact us Contact Us 1-604-504-7441 1-888-504-7441 Toll-Free Maps Ask a question Copy link ✓ Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More…"
