    "https://ufv.njoyn.com/CL3/xweb/xweb.asp?clid=56144&Page=JobDetails&Jobid=J1026-0875&BRID=365649&lang=1": {
      "title": "On-Call Instructor, Faculty of Applied & Technical Studies",
      "description": "Job postings > Careers | UFV.ca Future Students International Current Students Alumni Academic Calendar myUFV myClass Library UFV / Careers Job postings To display this page you need a browser with JavaScript support. Share Facebook X Email LinkedIn On-Call Instructor, Faculty of Applied & Technical Studies Industry Services & Part-time Trades Application deadline: November 30, 2026 Job Number: J1026-0875 Status: On-call Relief Open Positions: 1 Leave Replacement: No Campus(es): Chilliwack (CEP) Hours/Week: 35 % Full Time: 100 Total Months/Year: 12 Work Schedule: On-Call Position Salary Schedule: Sessional Hourly Schedule, Group B Salary: $45.74 - $69.05/Hour Job Summary The Faculty of Applied and Technical Studies at the University of the Fraser Valley invites applications from qualified trades professionals interested in future relief, temporary, and part-time instructional opportunities. Positions may be available across a variety of trades training programs and workforce development initiatives delivered at the Trades and Technology Centre, employer worksites, and partner locations throughout the region. Areas of Instruction The Faculty is seeking qualified instructors in the following trades: • Automotive Service Technician • Automotive Collision Repair and Refinish • Carpentry • Construction Electrician • Cooking • Heavy Mechanical Trades • Landscape Horticulture • Plumbing and Piping • Welding Qualifications Interprovincial Red Seal Certification or equivalent credential in the applicable trade. A minimum of five years of recent, directly related industry experience. Demonstrated ability to support student learning in classroom, shop, laboratory, workplace, or applied learning environments. Strong communication, interpersonal, and organizational skills. Experience delivering apprenticeship, foundation, continuing education, workforce training, or contract training programs is an asset. An Instructor Diploma, Provincial Instructor Diploma Program (PIDP), or equivalent instructional credential is preferred. Applicants without formal instructional training may be considered based on industry experience and qualifications. Experience working with diverse learners and industry partners is considered an asset. A satisfactory Criminal Record Check may be required for some assignments. About the Faculty The Faculty of Applied and Technical Studies prepares learners for careers in the skilled trades through industry-responsive programming, hands-on learning, and partnerships with employers, communities, and organizations throughout the Fraser Valley and beyond. How to Apply Please submit a resume and cover letter by the application deadline. About UFV The University of the Fraser Valley is located on the traditional territory of the Halq'eméylem-speaking peoples. We express our gratitude and respect for the honour of living and working in Stó:lo Tém:éxw (Stó:lo Land; Stó:lo World). In all that we do, UFV strives to support and honour the Stó:lo peoples goals of self-determination and well-being on these lands. A commitment to Indigenization and Reconciliation is core to our institutional Vision and Integrated Strategic Plan: IYAQAWTXW — which means House of Transformation. This commitment includes the goal of centering Indigenous ways of knowing throughout our organization, recognizing our responsibilities to community, and a multi-year plan to increase the number of Indigenous faculty, staff, and administrators working at UFV. UFV has campus locations in Abbotsford, Chilliwack, Mission, and Hope in the beautiful British Columbia, and in Chandigarh, India. Recognized as one of BC's top employers, UFV offers a combination of career and lifestyle benefits. Join a team of 1,400 passionate professionals who value integrity, inclusivity and excellence. At UFV, you will serve a vibrant community and shape the future of 15,000 students. Indigenization, equity, and diversity are essential to our work as a university. A diverse community fosters the inclusion of voices that have been historically underrepresented and marginalized. At UFV, we are committed to recruiting a diverse workforce that represents the community we proudly serve. We encourage applications from Indigenous peoples, members of groups that experience discrimination due to race, colour, place of origin, ancestry, and/or religion, persons who identify as women and 2SLGBTQ+, and persons with disabilities. We invite applicants to complete a confidential self-identification survey as part of the application process. All questions are voluntary, with an option to decline to answer. Information will be used to support efforts to broaden the diversity of the recruitment process, and results are not shared with the selection committee. Inquiries about the survey may be directed to careers@ufv.ca. Learn more about our commitment to diversity and inclusion. All qualified candidates are encouraged to apply; however, Canadians and permanent residents will be given priority. In an effort to be both environmentally and fiscally responsible, UFV will contact only candidates receiving an interview. We thank all applicants for considering UFV for employment. Shortlisted applicants may be required to undergo a criminal record check and/ or a verification of their education credentials. UFV is committed to the principle of equity in employment. Please note: you should receive a confirmation email once you have successfully applied to this position. If you do not, please contact the Njoyn Help Desk at webhelp.njoyn or 1-877-427-7717 Monday to Friday 8am to 8pm (EST). Are you interested in this job? Job Opportunities Career Alert My Profile Help 1-604-854-4554 careers@ufv.ca Future students Academic Calendar Find your program How to Apply Book a tour Transfer credits Tuition & fees FAQs Help Ask a question A to Z websites Course Finder Directory IT Service Desk Reset your password myUFV Search Current Students Advising Centre Bookstore Register for courses Safe Student Community Shuttle bus Student services Timetables myClass About us Accreditation Careers at UFV Cascades Athletics Make a gift Events Human Resources News Contact us Contact Us 1-604-504-7441 1-888-504-7441 Toll-Free Maps Ask a question Copy link ✓ Thanks for sharing! Find any service AddToAny More…"
